"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 8.6 and an ISUP grade group 3 Gleason pattern from the prostatectomy specimen. Positive surgical margins are concerning findings. Conversely, there was no documented seminal vesicle invasion and no lymph node metastasis reported in the pathology. The presence of lymphovascular invasion adds to the risk profile. Missing information regarding subsequent postoperative PSA trajectory would significantly impact prognosis assessment. Further follow-up data is needed to refine risk stratification beyond the current pathological findings. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.13–61.69 months; its coverage has not been validated."
